{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/973626-masquerade-style-paths-in-2e","id":973626,"title":"Masquerade-style Paths in 2e?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-20T20:57:32-07:00","id":973626,"title":"Masquerade-style Paths in 2e?","content":"I'm wondering, has anyone experimented with doing something like Masquerade's paths/roads for Requiem, especially the 2e mechanics? I think it could be really interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:18:24-07:00","id":973638,"title":"","content":"I've done a lot of little translation things over the years, so I've played around with them. There are a few ways of doing it:<ul><li>Import Paths as is; let vampires take them on if they fall far enough in Humanity</li> <li>Use a Merit; basically, you get a breaking point bonus equal to your Path Merit, if appropriate to the Path.</li> <li>Make them into Touchstones; Paths are metaphysical pillars that guide certain inhumane vampires. Each dot in Path is the equivalent of a Touchstone; roleplay appropriately. You might give a bigger bonus than Touchstones, but maybe for a penalty on actions that don't follow the Path.</li> </ul><br /> That being said, because Humanity is more about maintaining the Masquerade now, Paths (being moral codes) aren't as necessary, to my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T22:10:03-07:00","id":973667,"title":"","content":"2e also has the bane trade off system, which needs to be taken into account with any sort of Path. You don't wan to short change characters that stick on Humanity but take a Bane with the Path system being outright superior.<br /> <br /> Another option on the Merit side of things is to have a Merit that lets each Bane protect you more broadly in the service of the Path, but get harsher if you go against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:43:08-07:00","id":973844,"title":"","content":"Noblesse Oblige in the Secrets of the Covenants play test is a 3 dot merit that let's you replace a touchstone with your job within the city. See <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1B3dwo3Dzg1h3BKf2gb7Am3NTS01Bu87lKPV46AtUySg/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...Sg/mobilebasic</a><br /> How would we need to modify it to do what we want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:56:43-07:00","id":973850,"title":"","content":"Something else I would take into account. Humanity isn't exactly a moral Guage so much as how do humans react to you and how well for you understand humans. <br /> <br /> By default I would likely skew the social die modifier for any on a path. Perhaps even flip it upside down. <br /> <br /> Path of the Beast for example I would probably give you no penalty if you got it to 1. Where as at 10 you would probably have a -5. <br /> <br /> Perhaps even other kindred may have social die penalties for some of them, as you just don't interact with other kindred like normal. <br /> <br /> Just some thoughts for consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}